Reminders in light of the 1Password breach:

1) Don't store seed phrases / private keys in password managers. The convenience will be your undoing.

2) Don't store 2FA or backup codes in password managers. This completely defeats the point of having a "second factor." It's frankly concerning that many managers offer to store 2FA passkeys now. 🤬

@zecpplus Nothing is perfect but it's a great option.

@s_carruthtx1 This is where it gets tricky. If you're using a passkey as your primary factor and then have a separate 2FA then it's fine to store than in the password manager. If you're using a password as your primary factor and a passkey as 2FA then it's NOT fine to store both in one place.

@tierotiero I recommend yubikeys for 2FA. They can store both TOTP secrets and passkeys.

